{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1133556-accents-and-the-well-traveled-elder","id":1133556,"title":"Accents and the well traveled elder.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-08-24T14:42:49-07:00","id":1133556,"title":"Accents and the well traveled elder.","content":"So after some apparently poor attempts at googling the science of accents, I thought I would see what others thought about how the accent of an elder would play out. <br /> <br /> To give a rather extreme example, the npc concept that got me thinking of this is a vampire embraced in Vienna in her mid 20s sometime in the early 16th century. She remained there for several decades before traveling around Europe until she came to a stop in London for a roughly 80 year torpor and after awakening made her way to the US where she has been for the past century. If she's never made any concious effort to change or conceal her accent what would it be like now?<br /> <br /> Would she sound mostly American with a hint of something foreign? Would she have an indistinguishable &quot;polyglot&quot; accent? If she did still mostly have her original accent would it be possible for somebody to place it as Austrian given how much a nation or cultures speech can can change of 500 years.<br /> <br /> Any idea on how to describe the accent of a centuries old monster?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1571-kamikazegerbil","name":"Kamikazegerbil","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1571_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-24T16:45:04-07:00","id":1133585,"title":"","content":"Separate your hypothesis and throw dice to figure out which one it is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-24T16:45:58-07:00","id":1133586,"title":"","content":"Have fun with it. But things to ask yourself about the character. What language does she &quot;think&quot; in? Does she cling to her native language and speech mode or does she try to blend in with her contemporaries? I lived near a woman who lived in the U. S. for over 30 years. She refused to speak any language but Tagalog. She would have her children and grandchildren translate for her but she understood English perfectly well. There's a security officer who works at my workplace who started 5 years ago and had a heavy German accent. Today its barely noticeable. I have a friend who spent the first 10 years of his life in Germany. He speaks with a southern accent today. I regularly deal with Spanish speaking customers who turn their Spanish accent off and on at will to try and bully us or con our managers into violating company policy regarding product services. I've never lived in New England, but I had elocution lessons for three years when I was younger and I'm told that I sound like I'm from New Hampshire or Vermont from people who lived up North. But down South they think I only have a faint Southern accent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-24T16:56:51-07:00","id":1133590,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1133556-accents-and-the-well-traveled-elder?p=1133586#post1133586\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I regularly deal with Spanish speaking customers who turn their Spanish accent off and on at will to try and bully us or con our managers into violating company policy regarding product services.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wait, what? How does that even work?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-24T17:17:31-07:00","id":1133595,"title":"","content":"&quot;You talk funny, Nash, where you from?&quot;<br /> &quot;Lots of different places.&quot;<br /> <b>Highlander</b><br /> <br /> In this case, I'd have her speak English with a mostly localised accent and a strong hint of English and a trace of other European accents, but if she speaks German she mostly slips back into a Renaissance Austrian speech pattern which would sound very strange to modern German speakers. Perhaps an Academics roll with a bonus for Language Merits could help listeners puzzle out some of her background.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Craig Oxbrow<br /> <b>The Trinity Continuum</b> freelancer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/221-craig-oxbrow","name":"Craig Oxbrow","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar221_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-24T17:30:18-07:00","id":1133600,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Craig Oxbrow</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1133556-accents-and-the-well-traveled-elder?p=1133595#post1133595\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;You talk funny, Nash, where you from?&quot;<br /> &quot;Lots of different places.&quot;<br /> <b>Highlander</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Funny you mention that-historical linguists have posited that that movie accidentally hit on how someone like that would have spoken in the case of Connor McCloud, at least in the use of phonetically speaking it.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Quick and fun look at that point, thought not explained in depth.<br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=_VQk1gVAznU\" data-code=\"_VQk1gVAznU\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/_VQk1gVAznU/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 08-24-2017, 09:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-24T17:39:13-07:00","id":1133605,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1133556-accents-and-the-well-traveled-elder?p=1133590#post1133590\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wait, what? How does that even work?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm answering this, not with the intention of derailing the thread, but as an anecdote to demonstrate how people are able to quickly change their speech patterns and language when it suits them.<br /> <br /> For me, they call asking for service for a particular piece of equipment. They may or may not have a faint accent in the first 3-5 minutes of conversation troubleshooting certainly not thick enough to where they are hard to understand. Then when they're told they may have to pay for the repair usually because the equipment is outside the warranty period, they ask for a technician who speaks Spanish. Officially in the United States, we do not provide customer support in Spanish. It does not matter if you individually speak and understand Spanish, we are not supposed to conduct company business on the phone in any language other than English for both legal and customer service evaluation purposes. When it is explained to them that we do not provide technical support in Spanish, they talk over you and repeat the question over and over again turning on a Spanish accent and using more and more Spanish words and pretending they don't understand you. If they get belligerent or start slinging Spanish profanities, policy is to notify the customer that you are turning the call over to a manager. And when the manager gets on the phone they immediately revert to English and frequently start trash talking the technician and launch into demands for free or discounted service.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-24T19:24:26-07:00","id":1133629,"title":"","content":"First. there is no way to sound American as there are at least 3 major dialects and many minor dialects of American English. The important questions that need answered would be when and where was English learned and what is the US timeline. If this person spent 100 years in the same state then they should sound like a local, normally. Only an elitist or hermit (some hyperbole) would not adapt, which could describe an elder or not. If the person traveled around the US then you might get Julia Roberts or Sandra Bullock as my best guess. No clue as to when London began to develop its own thing, but as far as accents go, Southern US and West Country/Southern England sound close, Southern US English comes from Southern England originally.<br /> <br /> It would be just as likely a switch to German, Bavarian or whatever they spoke in Vienna at the time as English with a German accent. People tend to adopt local linguistic idiosyncrasies and switch to native tongue and accent without pause. Rather than mixing accents you are more likely to get mixed words, but accents may become more pronounced with agitation. That is my experience with people that learned English later in life from Spanish. English is Germanic so there is less distance to go.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-24T19:26:03-07:00","id":1133630,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1133556-accents-and-the-well-traveled-elder?p=1133605#post1133605\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm answering this, not with the intention of derailing the thread, but as an anecdote to demonstrate how people are able to quickly change their speech patterns and language when it suits them.<br /> <br /> For me, they call asking for service for a particular piece of equipment. They may or may not have a faint accent in the first 3-5 minutes of conversation troubleshooting certainly not thick enough to where they are hard to understand. Then when they're told they may have to pay for the repair usually because the equipment is outside the warranty period, they ask for a technician who speaks Spanish. Officially in the United States, we do not provide customer support in Spanish. It does not matter if you individually speak and understand Spanish, we are not supposed to conduct company business on the phone in any language other than English for both legal and customer service evaluation purposes. When it is explained to them that we do not provide technical support in Spanish, they talk over you and repeat the question over and over again turning on a Spanish accent and using more and more Spanish words and pretending they don't understand you. If they get belligerent or start slinging Spanish profanities, policy is to notify the customer that you are turning the call over to a manager. And when the manager gets on the phone they immediately revert to English and frequently start trash talking the technician and launch into demands for free or discounted service.</div> </div> </div> </div>In my personal experience, one of the earliest things you try to learn of a language is how to insult others (it's a fun exercise), so if we give them the benefit of the doubt it'd be something that they've practiced more than asking &quot;where's the bathroom?&quot;. Literally I know a guy who's only command of German is &quot;Why don't you go play dolls with the aborted fetuses of your sister?&quot; in phonetic perfection.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-24T20:24:40-07:00","id":1133646,"title":"","content":"I imagine that they'd &quot;reset&quot; an accent in about a decade after waking from torpor. Any languages that they know that they don't regularly practice would most likely maintain their old accents. You could maybe link it to their Wits, a high Wits character would be able to shift accents pretty easily, but a personne of looe wits finden themselfs perchance in talken with an accente more ahome in th'tyme of Chaucer. <br /> <br /> (addendum, I've never read Chaucher, I apologise for the terrible bastardization above.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2291-gwyn-chan-r-gwyll","name":"Gwyn chan 'r Gwyll","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-24T20:36:03-07:00","id":1133650,"title":"","content":"Its also going to depend on the speakers they're around. Accents have a tendency to seep into your language from exposure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-25T03:08:10-07:00","id":1133715,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gwyn chan 'r Gwyll</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1133556-accents-and-the-well-traveled-elder?p=1133646#post1133646\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I imagine that they'd &quot;reset&quot; an accent in about a decade after waking from torpor. Any languages that they know that they don't regularly practice would most likely maintain their old accents. You could maybe link it to their Wits, a high Wits character would be able to shift accents pretty easily, but a personne of looe wits finden themselfs perchance in talken with an accente more ahome in th'tyme of Chaucer.<br /> <br /> (addendum, I've never read Chaucher, I apologise for the terrible bastardization above.)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This is an interesting point as , at least as of 2nd ed., torpor is this &quot;regenerative&quot; reset period after a vampire wakes again maleable and able to quickly adapt and catch on new things. So maybe the accent a particular vampire has is very influenced by the last time she went into torpor.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-25T10:06:23-07:00","id":1133845,"title":"","content":"I hadn't thought about that. I may work that in to my setting. &quot;As most vampires age, they tend to become more set in their ways. The elder speaks in an accent that no longer exists, prefers fashions decades out of date, is slightly fearful of computers, or neglects the danger inherent in a smart phone. The undead is increasingly, and more obviously, set apart from modern life. Torpor brings a mental reset, for a newly-wakened vampire is quicker to pick up on technology, customs, language \u2013 anything to help him blend in and survive the modern nights.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2203-corrigan","name":"Corrigan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-25T14:14:49-07:00","id":1133943,"title":"","content":"A lot of interesting replies. I was leaning towards the character sounding like a local, after a few responses, especially given her M.O. being meeting with the rich and powerful among mortals and getting them under her thumb. A more isolated or stubborn kindred might retain much of their original accent.<br /> <br /> The torpor point is a good one. The 2nd ed description definitely suggests their period of fast learning is to allow them to blend with their prey more easily so an accent reset fits in with that nicely. I like it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1571-kamikazegerbil","name":"Kamikazegerbil","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1571_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-25T15:52:33-07:00","id":1133973,"title":"","content":"Now I kind of want her to sound like this:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/kdemFfbS5H0?t=7s\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/kdemFfbS5H0?t=7s\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/kdemFfbS5H0?t=7s\" target=\"_blank\"> https://youtu.be/kdemFfbS5H0?t=7s </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I mean call me slow, but I had to listen to that twice to pick up everything she said and I can imagine that vampires less than tenth of your PC's age would have the same problem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}